:" ============================================================"
:" Differentiable Physics: Learn to Hit the Target"
:" ============================================================"
:" This example demonstrates using autograd to BACKPROPAGATE"
:" THROUGH A PHYSICS FORMULA to optimize initial conditions."
:" The gradient flows through the physics equations!"
:" "
:" Problem: Find the launch angle to hit a target."
:" Solution: Compute the landing position using physics,"
:" compute the miss distance, and use autograd to find"
:" the gradient with respect to launch angle."
:" "
:" Run with: kgpy --backend torch differentiable_physics.kg"
:" ============================================================"

.p("Differentiable Physics: Projectile Targeting")
.p("=============================================")
.p("")
.p("Goal: Find the launch angle to hit a target at x=50")
.p("Method: Backpropagate through physics equations!")
.p("")

:" Import from backend"
.bkf(["sin" "cos" "sqrt"])

:" Physics constants"
g::9.81          :" Gravity"
v0::25.0         :" Initial velocity"
v0sq::625.0      :" v0^2 precomputed"

:" Target position"
tgtX::50.0

:" Launch angle (this is what we optimize)"
angle::1.2       :" Initial guess: ~69 degrees (way off!)"

.pf("Target x: {}";tgtX)
.pf("Initial velocity: {}";v0)
.p("")

:" Projectile range formula: R = (v0^2 * sin(2*angle)) / g"
:" This computes where the projectile lands (y=0)"
range(angle)::{(v0sq*sin(2*angle))%g}

:" Loss = squared distance from target"
loss(angle)::{(range(angle)-tgtX)^2}

:" Initial state"
.pf("Initial angle (rad): {}";angle)
.pf("Initial angle (deg): {}";angle*57.3)
.pf("Initial range: {}";range(angle))
.pf("Initial miss: {}";sqrt(loss(angle)))
.p("")

:" ============================================"
:" GRADIENT DESCENT THROUGH PHYSICS!"
:" ============================================"

.p("Optimizing launch angle via gradient descent...")
.p("(Gradients computed through physics equations!)")
.p("")

lr::0.000003
epochs::300

:" Training step - update angle using gradient"
:" Constrain angle to valid range (0.1 to 1.4 radians)"
step(i)::{[grad];grad::loss:>angle;angle::(0.1|(angle-(lr*grad)))&1.4;0}

:" Progress printing"
printProg(epoch)::{.d("Epoch ");.d(epoch);.pf(": angle={} deg, range={}, miss={}";[;angle*57.3;range(angle);sqrt(loss(angle))])}

:" Training loop (run in batches of 30, print progress between batches)"
batch(n)::{step'!30;printProg(n*30)}
batch'!10

.p("")
.p("Optimization complete!")
.pf("Final angle (rad): {}";angle)
.pf("Final angle (deg): {}";angle*57.3)
.pf("Final range: {}";range(angle))
.pf("Final miss: {}";sqrt(loss(angle)))

.p("")
:" Analytical solutions for verification"
:" For range R = v0^2*sin(2*theta)/g = target"
:" sin(2*theta) = target*g/v0^2, so there are two angles:"
:" theta = 0.5*arcsin(target*g/v0^2)           (the flat shot)"
:" theta = 0.5*(pi-arcsin(target*g/v0^2))      (the lobbed shot)"
.pyf("math";["asin"])
sinTwice::(tgtX*g)%v0sq
flatAngle::0.5*asin(sinTwice)
lobAngle::0.5*(3.141592653589793-asin(sinTwice))
.pf("Analytical angle, flat shot (deg): {}";flatAngle*57.29577951308232)
.pf("Analytical angle, lobbed shot (deg): {}";lobAngle*57.29577951308232)
.p("(The guess of 1.2 rad is on the lobbed side, so descent finds the lobbed one.)")

.p("")
.p("The gradient propagated through physics equations!")
.p("This technique enables: robot control, game AI, scientific inverse problems")
